          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You might have seen the rangoli art form, in which regions of different shapes are beautifully coloured using rangoli powder."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.337,
            0.136,
            0.674,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.337,
                0.136,
                0.674,
                0.389
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.413,
            0.557,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Which of these rectangles requires more rangoli powder to be coloured, if the colouring is done evenly?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.475,
            0.558,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can answer this by counting the number of non-overlapping unit squares (squares of sidelength 1 cm in this case) that can be packed into each of the rectangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.409,
            0.845,
            0.568
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.562,
                0.409,
                0.845,
                0.568
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.567,
            0.557,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Clearly, the rectangle having"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.584,
            0.846,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sidelengths 7 cm and 4 cm contains 7 × 4 = 28 unit squares, and the rectangle having sidelengths 8 cm and 3 cm contains 8 × 3 = 24 unit squares."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.639,
            0.846,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, the rectangle of sidelengths 7 cm and 4 cm requires more powder to be coloured."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.688,
            0.847,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recall that we measure the area of a region by finding the number of unit squares (which can also be a fraction) whose area equals that of the given region."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.743,
            0.845,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen that the number of unit squares contained in a rectangle is given by the product of its length and width —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.323,
            0.795,
            0.672,
            0.817
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "A r e a \\; o f a \\; r e c t a n g l e = l e n g t h \\times w i d t h ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.837,
            0.846,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The areas of the rectangles as seen in the previous problem are generally written as 28 sq. cm and 24 sq. cm, or as 28 cm"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and 24 cm"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
